# The tones waited for in the process table's late entries (roadmap
# memory.md M1): tests/posix/late.c with LATE_TONE has the process at entry
# 16, then 22, play a tone of 400 ticks and be killed after half a second;
# the kill cuts the tone short (dev_tone_stop, os-server.md P15), so a tone
# of a tick then takes one. The server kept the tones waited for as a 16-bit
# mask, a bit an entry: past entry 15 the killed tone went on (E8: 376 ticks
# more).
program: none
define: TEST_POSIX_LATE
define: LATE_TONE
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
late: the tone of entry 16, killed, cut short: yes
late: the tone of entry 22, killed, cut short: yes
late: the tone of the table's last entry, killed, cut short: yes
late: done
